cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SOLIDIFY: A Real-Time, Browser-Based WebGPU Phase-Field Solidification Instrument"
message: "If you use SOLIDIFY in teaching, benchmarks, or research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Cai
    given-names: Frank
    affiliation: "Purdue University, West Lafayette, IN, USA"
    email: cai485@purdue.edu
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-0041-1459"
repository-code: "https://github.com/fronkt/solidify"
url: "https://solidify.frankcai.dev/"
abstract: >-
  SOLIDIFY is a zero-install, browser-native WebGPU phase-field laboratory for
  real-time 2D and 3D (up to 192^3 voxels) dendritic solidification, dilute-alloy
  microsegregation, foundry casting thermal analysis, and Arrhenius-coupled
  solid-state heat treatment. It pairs a qualitative multi-grain Kobayashi solver
  with a quantitative Karma-Rappel thin-interface solver featuring an anti-trapping
  current, a 118-element periodic alloy composer backed by cited binary invariants,
  Monte Carlo Potts grain growth with stored energy and Zener pinning, and an
  automated verification suite.
keywords:
  - phase-field modeling
  - solidification
  - dendritic growth
  - materials science education
  - WebGPU
  - alloy metallurgy
  - grain growth
  - heat treatment
license: MIT
